    "head_commit_message": "feat(native): snapshot tests cut from the digest's battles (spec 39 step 8d-i)\n\nA cut is a digest battle's state after a tick (the snapshot's bytes, its\nrun's label and the squads listed). `cuts::resumed` reads it back into a\nPlay and steps the next tick, fingerprinting the field and the squads as\neach lap ends; `laps::lap` now shows the squads to the watcher too.\n\nEight cuts from the standard digest's mirrors and clashes, chosen so that\nevery phase the battles act in changes the state in one, are committed\nunder native/rust/cuts/ (about 390 KB) and written by\n`breach_digest cuts=<dir>`. Cargo tests require each to still be the\nbattle's state and to step as recorded. 8d is split: the field logs'\ncuts, which must carry FieldPlay's state, are 8d-ii.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_011AyPi54GBMMXTnTmXqUXg1",
